Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:32:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] =?UTF-8?q?hottyterm:=20a=20touch=20drags=20what=20o?=
 =?UTF-8?q?pts=20out=20of=20panning=20(SPEC=20=C2=A79.1)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A touch that begins over a surface that takes the pointer there is the
surface's to decide (hotty_host_touch): every phase of it goes to
hotty-blitz, taps included, and none to the pointer. While it may still
drag, its moves wait; once it pans, the terminal scrolls with them from
where it began, the moves held included, and the lift ends the wheel
gesture; once it drags, its moves are the surface's. A second finger, or
the platform, cancels it, and GTK's drag begun again when that finger
lifts is the same touch. A touch over the cells, or one that only
focuses the split (hotty-focus-click = focus), is the terminal's as
before. hottyterm takes no long press, so it never sends one.

Upstream lines: 46 added, 5 of them changed signatures (gesture and
offset parameters), all in src/apprt/gtk/class/surface.zig; the logic is
in src/termio/hotty.zig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
